<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goms</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goms is the uppermost section of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley in the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, from the Rhône Glacier down to near Brig. It was one of the seven tenths (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenden">Zenden</a>) that ruled the Republic of the Valais and is now a district. Its villages of dark wooden houses form a German-speaking farming area.</p></div>
